          "paper_id": "15803282",
          "section": "abstract",
          "text": "The extremely low efficiency of human embryonic stem cell (hESC) derivation using somatic cell nuclear transfer (SCNT) limits its potential application.",
          "score": 0.639018177986145,
          "page": null,
          "sentence_indices": [],
          "source_version": null
        },
        {
          "passage_id": "15803282:abstract:447:636:820d7d5fe4f5",
          "paper_id": "15803282",
          "section": "abstract",
          "text": "Here we show that overexpression of a related H3K9me3 demethylase KDM4A improves human SCNT, and that, as in mice, H3K9me3 in the human somatic cell genome is an SCNT reprogramming barrier.",
          "score": 0.6340251564979553,
          "page": null,
          "sentence_indices": [],
          "source_version": null
        },
        {
          "passage_id": "4547102:abstract:0:162:42f8f0c4df7a",
          "paper_id": "4547102",
          "section": "abstract",
          "text": "Aberrant epigenetic reprogramming often results in developmental defects in somatic cell nuclear transfer (SCNT) embryos during embryonic genome activation (EGA).",
          "score": 0.6051872372627258,
          "page": null,
          "sentence_indices": [],
          "source_version": null
        },
        {
          "passage_id": "4547102:abstract:831:1038:08b59cb88f5a",
          "paper_id": "4547102",
          "section": "abstract",
          "text": "Our results thereby indicate that KDM4E can function as a crucial epigenetic regulator of EGA and as an internal defective factor responsible for persistent H3K9me3/2 barriers to SCNT-mediated reprogramming.",
          "score": 0.5536450147628784,
          "page": null,
          "sentence_indices": [],
          "source_version": null
        },
        {
          "passage_id": "14225271:abstract:218:428:fd065351dd5b",
          "paper_id": "14225271",
          "section": "abstract",
          "text": "Early nuclear reprogramming methods, such as somatic cell nuclear transfer (SCNT) and cell fusion, posed significant technical hurdles to precise dissection of the regulatory programmes governing cell identity.",
